  "content/metrics-baseline.json (rebaselined), content/korean/lines.jsonl, content/korean/review-status.json, content/translations/de_de-status.json, docs/book/src/quest-tree.md: regenerated by the gates and translate.py."
 ],
 "generatorWeaknesses": [
  "The concept `gate` (울타리 문) has no `covers`, unlike fence, door and sign. Only the oak gate is spoken as 울타리 문; every other gate says its full name (\"가문비나무 울타리 문\", one unknown word), and the validator refuses to teach `gate` for a spruce or birch gate (QuestScaffoldTest: \"the sentence word '울타리 문' does not describe the goal\"). The three gate steps teach the specific gen_*_fence_gate concepts instead.",
  "INTERACT_ENTITY has no verb for shearing, leashing, brushing or milking. With shears in hand a wolf is still \"쓰다듬으세요\" (pet), a sheep, rabbit or frog is \"먹이를 주세요\" (feed), whatever the HOLDING condition says. The shearing trail therefore collects the wool with ACQUIRE_ITEM under HOLDING shears and the wolf finale pets the wolf with shears in hand.",
  "Only 15 creatures can be anchors (villager, trader, golems, cow, pig, sheep, chicken, horse, donkey, llama, cat, wolf, fox, armor stand). Rabbit, frog, goat, turtle, bee, mule and parrot cannot be 앞/옆/뒤 anchors, so the frog and rabbit trails get their form-dependent steps from fences, water and fence rings instead.",
  "EQUIP is the player's four armour slots, so wolf armour is GIVE with method USE_WITH. It reads \"늑대에게 늑대 갑옷을 주세요\" (give wolf armour to a wolf), which says handing over, not putting on, and the verb 입히다 is not in the table. The same goes for the scute that repairs the armour.",
  "coverage.py reads 쓰다듬으세요 (PET) as 쓰다 (write or use), and 쓰다듬다 is not a lexicon word. PET sentences therefore count 쓰다 as met and as unknown; the wolf-armour finale only stays under one unknown word because the cat trail pets twice before it on the learner path.",
  "A SEQUENCE has no object, so the (verb, object) pair limit does not see its parts. GIVE carrot, wheat, salmon and cod and RIDE horse are at the limit of 3 already, which pushed the horse and cat finales into SEQUENCEs (apple then ride; fish then pet) and the donkey into the riding trail. That is legitimate -고 practice, but the pair metric no longer measures it.",
  "Items without a concept (슬라임볼, 수박씨) are spoken from names.json and work in GIVE and HOLDING, but cannot appear in `teach`, so the step teaches only the animal and the hint cannot gloss the item. The slimeball (and melon or beetroot seeds) are never glossed.",
  "A WAIT with NEAR_ENTITY puts the conditions in the order they are written in the JSON (\"개구리 세 마리 근처에서 밤에 십 초 동안…\" with NEAR first, \"밤에 늑대 세 마리 근처에서…\" with TIME first); the prefix order should be fixed in the sentence builder, not left to the author. I wrote TIME first everywhere.",
  "translate.py check treats the German \"auf\" as a relation giveaway even inside separable verbs (aufstellen, aufhängen, reite auf), so hidden-form steps use platzieren, anbringen and reite es."
 ],
 "openIssues": [
  "Reachability: the two wolf-armour trails need wolf armour, which is six armadillo scutes from an armadillo (savanna or badlands, brushed with a brush). Both parents are level 1, and the brief did not list them among the five unreachable advancements, so they stay at level 2. If ARCH decides the savanna trip is too far for week one or two, adv_husbandry_remove_wolf_armor and adv_husbandry_repair_wolf_armor are the candidates to move to level 3 (I did not change koreanLevel).",
  "Reachability: the lead (끈) in the frog trail needs a slimeball (a swamp slime at night) and string; the mangrove-swamp pond needs a mangrove swamp near the start. Frogs live in swamps and mangrove swamps, rabbits in meadows, wolves in forests and taigas, donkeys on plains and in savannas.",
  "Sensors: the wolf finale only checks an interaction with shears held, not that the armour came off; the repair finale waits ten seconds near a wolf because the sensor cannot see armour durability. MOUNT asks for 2000 ms in the saddle, and an untamed horse or donkey can throw the rider sooner; feeding it first (the apple, the hay) raises the temper.",
  "The five advancements that needed things beyond level 2 are rebuilt as day-week animal trails with new titles, none moved: froglights is now 개구리 연못의 밤 (A Night at the Frog Pond), kill_axolotl_target is 양털 깎는 날 (Shearing Day), allay_deliver_cake_to_note_block is 동물들의 노래 (A Song for the Animals), feed_snifflet is 돼지 우리 (The Pig Pen) and plant_any_sniffer_seed is 토끼 밭 (The Rabbit Patch). Their ids and badges are kept, so the vanilla advancement no longer matches the trail; their lang titles are new.",
  "송아지 (calf) is not in names.json; the official ko_kr has 새끼 돼지, 병아리, 망아지 and 새끼 늑대 but no baby cow. I used the standard word 송아지 in one finale; the pig finale uses 새끼 돼지.",
  "물고기 as a watched or fed entity (wave 8) is not used: WATCH cod is at the pair limit, and the cat trail feeds a fish inside a SEQUENCE instead.",
  "BATCH-014 slack: the verb-object pairs at exactly 3 that I touch are CRAFT note_block, GIVE apple and HANG white_banner. duplicateSignatures went from 8 to 6 (none of mine), unknownOverOneShare from 0.052206 to 0.051534."
 ]
